# Axebane Ferox: "Ward-Collect evidence 4." If the player whose spell targeted it cannot exile cards with total mana value 4 or
# greater from their graveyard, they can't choose to collect evidence at all (CR 701.59b), so the ward counters the spell and
# nothing is asked. Bot2 holds priority and casts a Lightning Strike and a Lightning Bolt at Bot1 and then a second Bolt at the
# Ferox, so the stack holds three spells and the ward trigger goes above them: Bot2's graveyard has only its Black Lotus (mana
# value 0), the spells on the stack count for nothing, so the ward counters the Bolt that targeted - the top spell, not another
# - and the Ferox (4/4) is undamaged while the other two spells resolve. Nothing is exiled.

